# Copy to .env and fill in. .env is gitignored.
#
# THEIR PROVIDER, NOT OURS. Use whichever provider you already hold a key for -- a kit that
# hardcodes one vendor is broken for most of the people who fork it. PROVIDER picks the adapter,
# MODEL picks the model behind it, and swapping either is this file plus one more run.
#
# ⚑ YOU DO NOT NEED A KEY TO SEE THIS KIT WORK, AND HERE THAT IS MORE THAN A COURTESY. Unlike the
# text-to-SQL kit next door, this one has a REAL free half: the corpus is generated by
# tools/build_corpus.py from a fixed seed, and the whole deterministic matcher -- normalisation,
# blocking, the weighted similarity score, the threshold sweep, all five outcomes -- is pure code.
#
#     python3 tools/build_corpus.py     # the corpus, byte-identical every time
#     python3 -m evals.baseline         # a WORKING matcher, scored, 0 calls, $0.00
#     python3 -m src.app                # the panel, every score computed locally
#
# A key is needed only to ask the model about a pair (one call per Judge click) or to run the eval.
#
# ⚠︎ IF THIS KIT SITS INSIDE THE KITS REPO, IT ALREADY INHERITS THE ROOT .env AND THEREFORE A LIVE
# KEY. "I have not configured anything yet" is not the same as "nothing can spend". Check
# /api/status, or `python3 -m evals.run --dry-run`, before touching anything that calls out.

PROVIDER=openai-compatible
BASE_URL=https://api.openai.com/v1
API_KEY=
MODEL=

# No EMBED_MODEL: nothing is embedded. Records are compared field by field, and the candidate pairs
# come from cheap blocking keys rather than from a vector index -- which is also why this kit's
# breaks_at_scale limit is about pair counts, not about context windows.
